        <p>Kathakali emanated in the 16th century taking inspiration from  Koodiyattam, a remnant of ancient Sanskrit drama and a 12th century Sanskrit  musical called GeethaGovindam. It improved and evolved continuously. At the  actor level, it was defined by Premkumar(ex Shantiniketan)  as the outward expression of inward  feelings through the medium of bodily movements. But, there is more to it. It  mixes the best of literature, opera, dance, epics, music, percussion, makeup,  costumes, facial expressions, body movements and a philosophy which says-If you  have conquered your ego(as cause of egotism), you have conquered all. Kathakali continues to  evolve..... While Kathakali performances are taking place throughout the world,  there is no documentation with respect to these performances. This website is a  sincere attempt to fill this gap. Hereby we wish to serve Kathakali, its  artists and its enthusiastic audience. </p>
      <p class="style2">If you possess a notice of any Kathakali performance which  is to be staged in your locality or have definite information about staging  such an event, we request you to enter the details of the event through the  facility we are offering. <strong>By this you are helping someone</strong> to see Kathakali. You can also view all previous entries through the facility.  In that case please reconfirm the event through telephone or other means before  you proceed since this is a purely interactive website and no guarantee is  given for the website entries.<span class="style10"> We expect best cooperation from you….&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></p>
